-- Gandham, Akshatai & Pushpam: meaning was the old sandal / rice / flower verses; philosophy listed six flowers (jaji, champaka, shatapatra, kalhara) the mantra does not name.
update public.pooja_steps set meaning_en = 'Blended with camphor and sandal, with musk and kumkumam: receive today every fragrance, you who grant all that is auspicious. To Sri Varalakshmi, salutations: I apply the sandal, and over it I offer turmeric powder. Grains of rice, moon-white, glossy as pearls: receive these akshatai, goddess, beloved of the lotus-eyed one. With mandara, parijata and lotus, with ketaki, water-lily and patala, with jasmine, jati and vakula flowers I worship you. I offer the garland, and I worship you with flowers.', updated_at = now()
 where pooja_id = 'varalakshmi_vratham' and step_title_en = 'Gandham, Akshatai & Pushpam'
   and meaning_en is distinct from 'Blended with camphor and sandal, with musk and kumkumam: receive today every fragrance, you who grant all that is auspicious. To Sri Varalakshmi, salutations: I apply the sandal, and over it I offer turmeric powder. Grains of rice, moon-white, glossy as pearls: receive these akshatai, goddess, beloved of the lotus-eyed one. With mandara, parijata and lotus, with ketaki, water-lily and patala, with jasmine, jati and vakula flowers I worship you. I offer the garland, and I worship you with flowers.';
update public.pooja_steps set philosophy_en = 'Mandara, parijata, lotus, ketaki, water-lily, patala, jasmine, jati, vakula. The verse names nine flowers, two of them from the gardens of heaven, and expects none of them in particular; it is a way of saying "the best that is in the garden".', updated_at = now()
 where pooja_id = 'varalakshmi_vratham' and step_title_en = 'Gandham, Akshatai & Pushpam'
   and philosophy_en is distinct from 'Mandara, parijata, lotus, ketaki, water-lily, patala, jasmine, jati, vakula. The verse names nine flowers, two of them from the gardens of heaven, and expects none of them in particular; it is a way of saying "the best that is in the garden".';

-- Anga Pooja: instruction_ta said fourteen names and a fifteenth for the body; there are twenty-four.
